{
  "$comment_purpose": "Few-shot example library for the Language Understanding parser (backend/prompts/parser_prompt.txt). Every entry pairs a realistic household-robot instruction with the exact JSON a correct parse of it should produce, matching schemas.task.SingleTask / MultiTask (backend/schemas/task.py) field-for-field. These examples are disjoint from the five worked examples embedded directly in parser_prompt.txt -- duplicating them here would test nothing a prompt review couldn't already see, and this file exists specifically to cover categories broader than what fits readably inline in the prompt itself.",
  "$comment_responsibility": "Provide diverse, realistic, schema-valid VALID commands only. Anti-patterns (what the parser must never produce) live in negative_examples.json; ambiguous/unusual inputs live in edge_cases.json; this file is the 'normal operation, wide category coverage' set.",
  "$comment_consumers": "A future Language Agent (Phase 3.4) may sample from this file for dynamic few-shot prompt construction. Phase 3.6 (Testing & Benchmarking) may use it as a smoke-test set distinct from the formal evaluation benchmarks in datasets/language/evaluation/. Prompt engineers reviewing a parser_prompt.txt change should re-check outputs against every category here before merging.",
  "$schema_version": "1.0.0",
